================================================================================
S219: duodecimal observer-extension / cut-payload synthesis
================================================================================
1. SHIFTED ROOTED-PERSPECTIVE LADDER
   m  U(m)  P(m)  U(m+1)  defect  P/U(m+1)  defect/U(m+1)  root_tax=mU-P
   1     1     1       1       0           1               0               0
   2     1     2       2       0           1               0               0
   3     2     4       4       0           1               0               2
   4     4    12      12       0           1               0               4
   5    12    48      56       8         6/7             1/7              12
   6    56   296     456     160       37/57           20/57              40

   First failure window:
     P(5) = 48 = 4 * 12
     U(6) = 56 = 4 * 12 + 8
     48 + 12 = 60, so the exact count is not 48+12.
     U(6) = P(5) + U(5) - U(4) = 48 + 12 - 4
     defect = U(6)-P(5) = 8 = U(5)-U(4)
     P(5)/U(6) = 6/7; defect/U(6) = 1/7
     U(5)/U(6) = 3/14; U(4)/U(6) = 1/14
     Denominator-14 form: 12/14 + 3/14 - 1/14 = 1.

   Recurrence guardrail:
     The identity U(6)=P(5)+U(5)-U(4) is exact at the first failure.
     It is not a stable recurrence: U(7)-P(6)=160, but U(6)-U(5)=44.

2. THE DOZEN BRIDGE P(4) = U(5) = SC(6)
   object                                      value  fraction_of_U6
   P(4): rooted 4-perspectives                         12          3/14
   U(5): 5-tournament isomorphism classes              12          3/14
   SC(6): self-converse 6-classes                      12          3/14
   P(5): rooted 5-perspective cache                    48           6/7
   U(6)-P(5): first observer-cut defect                 8           1/7
   U(4): overlap subtracted by inclusion-exclusion      4          1/14
   U(6): full 6-class quotient                         56             1

   Exact relations:
     P(4)=U(5)=SC(6)=12
     P(5)=5*U(5)-SC(6)=60-12=48
     U(6)=5*U(5)-U(4)=60-4=56
     U(6)-P(5)=SC(6)-U(4)=12-4=8
     Reading: the dozen is a control/fold slice; the additive defect is the
     dozen after quotienting out the four-class overlap.

