   edge_flips_from_input_order:
     observer_extension_cut_payload > cross_sector_orientation_word

BOTTOM LINE
  The dozen is not the first-failure additive defect.  It is a reusable
  control slice: P(4)=U(5)=SC(6)=12, source/sink diagonal words each give
  12 slices at 5->6, and K_{3,4} is the first 12-line rectangle carrier.
  The exact first-failure arithmetic is duodecimal inclusion-exclusion:
  U(6)=48+12-4, or 12/14 + 3/14 - 1/14 = 1.  The missing 8 is the dozen
  minus the four-class overlap, i.e. observer-extension cut payload after
  controlled forgetting.
